test.yaml:15:15: "pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish@76f52bc884231f62b9a034ebfe128415bbaabdfc" publishes to PyPI with the OIDC token of the job ("id-token: write"), and the job has no "environment:". tie the trusted publisher to an environment and add it to the job (with required reviewers if you can), so that a run that someone else started cannot publish on its own [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:15:15: "pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish@76f52bc884231f62b9a034ebfe128415bbaabdfc" publishes to PyPI with the OIDC token of the job ("id-token: write"), but the job also checks out the repository and runs "pip install build" before it, so that code and the code of its dependencies can use the token as well. build the package in another job without "id-token: write", pass it on as an artifact, and publish from a job that only downloads and publishes it [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:24:41: "npm publish" publishes to npm with the OIDC token of the job ("id-token: write"), and the job has no "environment:". tie the trusted publisher to an environment and add it to the job (with required reviewers if you can), so that a run that someone else started cannot publish on its own [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:24:41: "npm publish" publishes to npm with the OIDC token of the job ("id-token: write"), but the job also checks out the repository and runs "npm ci" before it, so that code and the code of its dependencies can use the token as well. build the package in another job without "id-token: write", pass it on as an artifact, and publish from a job that only downloads and publishes it [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:50:14: "twine upload" publishes to PyPI with the OIDC token of the job ("id-token: write"), and the job has no "environment:". tie the trusted publisher to an environment and add it to the job (with required reviewers if you can), so that a run that someone else started cannot publish on its own [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:61:25: action "pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish@76f52bc884231f62b9a034ebfe128415bbaabdfc" is told not to publish attestations ("attestations: false"), although it does by default: they let the users of the package check where and how it was built. remove the input [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:70:15: "rust-lang/crates-io-auth-action@e919bc7605cde86df457cf5b93c5e103838bd879" publishes to crates.io with the OIDC token of the job ("id-token: write"), and the job has no "environment:". tie the trusted publisher to an environment and add it to the job (with required reviewers if you can), so that a run that someone else started cannot publish on its own [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:85:14: "npm publish" publishes to npm with the long-lived credential NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, although the job can request an OIDC token ("id-token: write"). prefer trusted publishing: configure the trusted publisher of the package on npmjs.com and grant the permission "id-token: write", then no token is needed [use-trusted-publishing]
